;; WS-E generality sibling #1 — declared ownership map for the PROOF
;; peripheral's phase-output contract (CR-1..8). Authored by claude-7
;; (2026-08-15) from proof.clj + proof_shapes.clj + reader greps; checked by
;; futon3c.diagramprover.wiring under contract (c).
;;
;; TWO FINDINGS ESTABLISHED DURING AUTHORING (recorded here because the map
;; must be truthful, and truth is what surfaced them):
;; 1. :enforce-required-outputs? is NOT set in proof-domain-config — the
;;    engine's output gate is opt-in (cycle.clj), only problem.clj opts in.
;;    The CR-1..8 required-outputs contract therefore gates nothing at
;;    advance time. There is deliberately NO :required-outputs-gate box in
;;    this map: declaring one would assert a reader that does not act.
;;    Fix is one line but changes proof-cycle behavior — flagged to the
;;    proof peripheral's owners, not applied here.
;; 2. proof_logic.clj holds a PRIVATE DUPLICATE of phase-order and
;;    phase-required-outputs, and the copies have DRIFTED: the duplicate is
;;    9 phases, missing :target-check and its three outputs (:proof-plan
;;    :formal-alignment :target-sanity). The duplicate is the copy that is
;;    actually consumed (query-missing-phase-outputs -> :missing-phase-outputs),
;;    so the only live output-checking reads the stale contract while the
;;    canonical one gates nothing (finding 1). First draft of this map claimed
;;    :saved? had no reader — the conformance check flagged its occurrence in
;;    proof_logic, which is how the duplicate was found. (The authoring grep
;;    was broken for :saved? — \b after ? — the checker's lookahead was not.)
;;
;; Reader boxes are declared at keyword-occurrence granularity (the checker's
;; documented textual limitation): same-name keywords in unrelated namespaces
;; (bridge.clj :approach etc.) are NOT declared as cycle-field readers.
;; :phases is not stored here — the snapshot runner assoc's it from the live
;; proof-shapes config at check time.
{:spec/id :proof-peripheral-live
 :boxes
 [{:box/id :cycle-advance-payload
   :site {:ns "futon3c.peripheral.proof-shapes"}
   :writes [:blocker-id :approach :proof-plan :formal-alignment :target-sanity
            :artifacts :validation-artifacts :classification :rationale
            :ledger-changes :saved? :gates-passed]}
  {:box/id :proof-logic
   ;; reads via its own DUPLICATED (and drifted) contract copy — see note 2.
   ;; :saved? included: consumed through the duplicate's :commit entry.
   ;; :target-check's three outputs deliberately absent: the duplicate does
   ;; not know they exist, which is the drift.
   :site {:ns "futon3c.peripheral.proof-logic"}
   :reads [:blocker-id :approach :artifacts :validation-artifacts
           :classification :rationale :ledger-changes :saved? :gates-passed]}
  {:box/id :apm-work-queue
   :site {:ns "futon3c.agents.apm-work-queue"}
   :reads [:proof-plan :formal-alignment :target-sanity :artifacts
           :classification]}]}
